        answer: "From on-site systems engineered for the site: a well with treatment, storage, and backup-powered pumping for water, and a county-health-department-approved septic or advanced-treatment system for wastewater. The engineer sizes both for peak lodge occupancy plus fire protection demands, sites them for the high water table and setbacks, and provides the operations manuals the county requires.",
